{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/564950-generational-differences-amoung-werewolves","id":564950,"title":"generational differences amoung werewolves","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-22T20:54:46-07:00","id":564950,"title":"generational differences amoung werewolves","content":"Since Dark Eras is coming, I figure that maybe we can come up with some differences between the different generations of werewolves in terms of tribal culture and what tribes are most popular with different generations, what kinds of totems they prefer ,how they organize their packs and such things and how the shadow was influenced by the culture of each decade.<br /> <br /> I figure Gen X werewolves who came of age in the 80s are very capitalistic, often having totems relating to business and the idea of the Corporate predator. Iron masters, Storm lords, and Ivory claws of that era saw a large number of &quot;Beast of the Boardroom&quot; types entering the tribes and bringing large amounts of wealth with them, many packs of Gen X were run as businesses.<br /> <br /> Millennial werewolves who were kids in the 80s are similar, due to youth media like ghostbusters that enshrined business owners and vilified big government (think of the EPA guy and how his subplot is never really resolved), but also have a militaristic streak as a result of spending their childhood's watching GI Joe, star wars and other media of the 80s that had a morally reductive view of evil and warfare, thus leading to a number of Blood Talons known for seeing violence as the only real solution to conflict, which contributed to the violence of the Brethren war.<br /> <br /> 90s kid Millennials are mostly split between Hunters in Darkness and Predator Kings (due to the prevalence of media with environmentalist themes in that decade.) but also had more iron masters then any previous generation.<br /> <br /> Fire touched suffer in recruitment among Boomers and Millennials due to their general distrust of organized religion.<br /> <br /> The high divorce rates among the parents of Gen X , a result of no fault divorce being made law in the late 70s, wrecked havoc on the Ivory Claws that they still have yet to recover from. Many arranged marriages between Ivory Claws of the boomer generation ended in bitter divorces in the 80s and 90s and the resulting lack of faith in marriage has led many young claws to have unrecorded one night stands that make keeping the tribes genealogical records that much harder. Support of homosexual couples among young claws has also risen as a result, since they have a more cynical view of marriage, and Luna's Embrace (obviously called something different by the pure) is often used by young same sex claw couples as a means of reproduction, a practice is that is controversial among the older claws.<br /> <br /> anyone else got some ideas?<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> As for the shadow.<br /> <br /> The shadow in the 80s was dominated by spirits of greed and excess. Bale hounds of that stripe were very powerful in that decade.<br /> <br /> In the 90s, the end of the cold war led to the collapse of the spirit courts of the soviet union. The former USSR was a place where a young werewolf could carve out quite a territory.<br /> <br /> Shadow in america in the 90s was filled with spirits of milleinal panic and paranoia, feeding off the Y2K panic and the antigovenment militia boom. The mulitculturalsim movement led to some spirit courts fusing together. For some odd reason, there was never a confirmed sighting of a post-modernism spirit in the 90s. they were always &quot;packmate of a friend of a packmate of an ex-lover&quot; stories, which always portrayed the spirits of post modernism to be servants of the idigam.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/